From 4e5c069fafc4049f2e1c583275e5202b9fbcb4e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Neuffer <neuffer@neuffer.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:14:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] poe: RTL8238C PoE for the keepLiNK KP-9000-9XHPML-X V1.2 on
 current main

Stopgap until #712 is rebased onto main; not meant to be merged as is.
This is the net change of three pieces of work, unchanged, applied onto
main 58dccd6:

- hlyi: PoE infrastructure (#712)
- themmm: RTL8238C driver (966db0d)
- scow92: second PSE image and checked I2C reads (v2 patch in #712)

The driver files are byte-identical to that combination as built on
themmm's branch. The only new part is the glue for main's
machines.json registry: a machine entry may carry "poe_chip"; the
Makefile then reads it with jq, passes -DMACHINE_POE_CHIP and compiles
machine/pcb/<pcb>__POE.c (the PCB file plus its poe_cfg) instead of the
PCB file. Only KEEPLINK_KP_9000_9XHPML_X sets it. #712's RealHD board
entry is not carried over.
